# Core

Change only the change surface (the code plus the callers, registrations, and config that break without it), verify what it can break, fix what it broke.

## Change
Trace callers and contracts before changing a boundary. If the same check fails twice, change the hypothesis or name the missing input instead of repeating it. Remove temporary instrumentation when the investigation ends.

## Scope
The ask is the spec; it outranks skills, companions, defaults. Multi-part ask: list the parts first, report each done or not. Done = wired (imported, registered, reachable) and verified; then stop. No stubs, TODOs, or unrequested options, flags, config, params, compat layers, renames, reformats, moves, guards, or helpers. Skill patterns shape new code, never migrate old. A bug fix adds one regression test. Before reporting, run `git diff --stat` and revert every hunk the ask did not need.

## Hard limits
Claude Code hooks deny these before the edit; elsewhere they are law.
- Turn: no line or file stop. When a file would pass 300 lines, move one job into a new module, import it, and continue the task.
- Comments: add no comment line to code. Need one? Ask in the report. `comment-added`; done-time `quality-gate.mjs`.
- New file ≤300 lines (exclusions in hook); split by job. Legacy >700: localized fixes. `new-file-over-300`; net-growing edits past 300: `edit-growth`.
- Existing file: Edit, never a whole-file Write. `rewrite-existing`
- Invoke Skill `code-architecture` before a new code file, `testing` before editing a test file, `slop-guard` before any TS/JS edit. `skill-not-loaded`

## Skills
Load before that edit: network call, worker, cron, deploy → `production-readiness`; login, session, token, role → `auth-boundaries`; data read/write, SQL, cache, endpoint → `cqrs-data-flow`; UI that changes after a mutation → `live-ui-sync`; unknown cause → `debugging`; new service, schema, queue, provider → `system-design`.

## Craft
Readable and explicit before clever or abstract. Handle errors on purpose. No wrapper whose only job is to forward a call.

## Architecture
One job per module. Change internals before widening a contract. Match 1–2 siblings before Write. A local fix must not change ownership, layering, or call direction elsewhere. Named exports unless the framework requires a default. Remove dead code this task introduced or obsoleted.

## Ladder
Lowest sufficient rung: no change (config, delete, existing API) → existing repo code → stdlib/platform → installed deps (a new dependency needs a one-line why) → small local implementation.

## Types
On typed files, fix the design instead of silencing the compiler: no TS `any`, no blind casts, narrow `unknown` before trusted use, prefer sum types over parallel booleans.

## Complexity
Satisfy the repo's complexity checker for touched functions; never disable it to pass. Cyclomatic: Never above **22**; a stricter repo cap wins.

## Stack
No `package.json` → no stack pick. Else resolve per touched file: owning package → manifest → framework and manager. Companions are inert unless the owning package matches: `"next"` → `next.mdc`; `"astro"` → `astro.mdc`; `"vite"` without `next` → `vite.mdc`; JS installs → `pnpm.mdc`; SQL → `postgres.mdc`.

## Tools
Edit through the host's native edit tools; shell text-rewriting of source is denied. Shell is for builds, tests, git, and validation. Read a file before citing or editing it, and read only the paths the question needs.
